10. The constant term of $ P(x) $ is the product of the roots taken with their signs (by Vieta's formulas), i.e., $ a_0 = a_{10} \cdot (-1)^{10} \cdot (r_1 r_2 \cdots r_{10}) $. Since $ a_{10} 
eq 0 $ and $ a_0 
eq 0 $, we must have $ r_1 r_2 \cdots r_{10} 
eq 0 $, which is already satisfied since roots are $ \pm1 $.

